      ******************************************************************
      *  Testsuite : COTRN02C ADD-TRANSACTION
      *  Program-under-test : app/cbl/COTRN02C.cbl
      *
      *  Exercises COTRN02C's add-transaction CICS transaction by
      *  mocking ONLY the CICS-API boundary (CALL 'DFHEI1').  Internal
      *  paragraphs are NEVER mocked; every TESTCASE PERFORMs a
      *  production paragraph LIVE per AAP Section 0.10.1.
      *
      *  Test categories (6 testcases, off-platform-reachable subset)
      *  -----------------------------------------------------------
      *    TC1 - RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN substitutes default COSGN00C
      *          (AAP TC6 "PF3 exits without WRITE" pathway).
      *    TC2 - INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS clears 14 BMS fields + WS-MSG
      *          (lines 762-779).  Pure WS side effects.
      *    TC3 - VALIDATE-INPUT-KEY-FIELDS rejects empty ACCT/CARD
      *          via WHEN OTHER (lines 224-229).
      *    TC4 - VALIDATE-INPUT-DATA-FIELDS rejects empty Type CD via
      *          FIRST WHEN clause (lines 252-257); AAP TC2 align.
      *    TC5 - VALIDATE-INPUT-DATA-FIELDS rejects empty Amount via
      *          FIFTH WHEN clause (lines 276-281); AAP TC3 align.
      *    TC6 - CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN INITIALIZE + SEND-TRNADD;
      *          MAIN-PARA WHEN DFHPF4 destination.
      *
      *  Test user: USER0001 (AAP 0.10.2).  AAP TC1/TC4/TC5 (full
      *  happy / duplicate-key / invalid-date) deferred to MOCK CICS
      *  support (DFHRESP undefined off-platform; CSUTLDTC not linked).
      *  References: AAP 0.10.1, 0.5.1, 0.10.2, 0.4.1;
      *  app/cbl/COTRN02C.cbl L107-466, L500-779;
      *  app/cpy/{COCOM01Y, CVTRA05Y}.cpy; app/cpy-bms/COTRN02.CPY;
      *  tests/stubs/{STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy, DFHEI1.cbl};
      *  tests/cobol-check/{COUSR03C, COUSR02C}.cut (exemplars).
      *
      *  DFHEI1 fail-loudly safety net (QA CP4 Phase 5.2 anchor).
      *  Runner-script Step 5 injects EXTERNAL field declarations
      *  into merged WS; BEFORE-EACH resets WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-
      *  CALLED for per-testcase isolation of the safety-net flag.
      ******************************************************************
       COPY STUB-ABEND-FLAG.

       TESTSUITE 'COTRN02C ADD-TRANSACTION'.

      ******************************************************************
      *  BEFORE-EACH -- per-testcase isolation reset.
      *
      *  Restores deterministic baseline state so every TESTCASE
      *  starts from a known, identical configuration.  cobol-check
      *  resets MOCK invocation counters automatically between
      *  TESTCASEs; this block resets the application working-
      *  storage fields and shared structures the production code
      *  reads or writes:
      *
      *    WS-VARIABLES        WS-PGMNAME='COTRN02C', WS-TRANID=
      *                        'CT02', WS-TRANSACT-FILE='TRANSACT',
      *                        WS-ACCTDAT-FILE, WS-CCXREF-FILE,
      *                        WS-CXACAIX-FILE, WS-ERR-FLG='N',
      *                        WS-RESP-CD, WS-REAS-CD, WS-USR-
      *                        MODIFIED, WS-TRAN-AMT, WS-TRAN-DATE,
      *                        WS-ACCT-ID-N, WS-CARD-NUM-N, WS-TRAN-
      *                        ID-N, WS-TRAN-AMT-N, WS-TRAN-AMT-E,
      *                        WS-DATE-FORMAT (production lines 35-60
      *                        VALUE clauses re-applied).
      *    CSUTLDTC-PARM       Date-conversion parm group used by
      *                        CALL 'CSUTLDTC' (production lines 62-
      *                        69).  Not exercised by TC1-TC6 but
      *                        reset for forward-compatibility.
      *    CARDDEMO-COMMAREA   COCOM01Y plus CDEMO-CT02-INFO extension
      *                        fields (CT02 suffix unique to this
      *                        transaction; sister COUSR0xC programs
      *                        own CU0x suffix blocks).
      *    TRAN-RECORD         CVTRA05Y group; target of ADD-
      *                        TRANSACTION's INITIALIZE / MOVE /
      *                        WRITE sequence (production lines 450-
      *                        466).  Reset for forward-compatible
      *                        extensions that PERFORM ADD-
      *                        TRANSACTION end-to-end.
      *    ACCOUNT-RECORD      CVACT01Y group (production line 89).
      *    CARD-XREF-RECORD    CVACT03Y group; target of READ-
      *                        CXACAIX-FILE / READ-CCXREF-FILE.
      *    COTRN2AI            BMS input map (14 input fields plus
      *                        paired length / attribute fields)
      *                        from cpy-bms/COTRN02.CPY.
      *    RETURN-CODE         implicit special-register reset.
      *
      *  After clearing, BEFORE-EACH seeds the COMMAREA with the
      *  USER0001 regular-user identity per AAP Section 0.10.2.
      *  CDEMO-FROM-* fields default to 'COMEN01C' / 'CM00' so the
      *  RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN paragraph has a non-empty origin to
      *  reflect back into the COMMAREA -- except in TC1, which
      *  deliberately wipes CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM to exercise the line-
      *  502 default-substitution branch.
      ******************************************************************
       BEFORE-EACH
            INITIALIZE WS-VARIABLES ALL TO VALUE
            INITIALIZE CSUTLDTC-PARM
            INITIALIZE CARDDEMO-COMMAREA
            INITIALIZE TRAN-RECORD
            INITIALIZE ACCOUNT-RECORD
            INITIALIZE CARD-XREF-RECORD
            INITIALIZE COTRN2AI
            MOVE ZERO       TO RETURN-CODE
            MOVE 'N'        TO WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED
            MOVE 'USER0001' TO CDEMO-USER-ID
            MOVE 'U'        TO CDEMO-USER-TYPE
            MOVE 'COMEN01C' TO CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM
            MOVE 'CM00'     TO CDEMO-FROM-TRANID
       END-BEFORE.

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC1 -- RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN substitutes default and XCTLs
      *
      *  Drives RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN (production lines 500-511).
      *  Destination of MAIN-PARA's WHEN DFHPF3 branch (lines 136-
      *  143) -- the AAP-aligned "PF3 exits without WRITE" pathway
      *  -- and the EIBCALEN = 0 initial-entry branch.  Production
      *  executes:
      *      IF CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM = LOW-VALUES OR SPACES   (line 502)
      *          MOVE 'COSGN00C' TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM      (line 503)
      *      END-IF
      *      MOVE WS-TRANID    TO CDEMO-FROM-TRANID       (line 505)
      *      MOVE WS-PGMNAME   TO CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM      (line 506)
      *      MOVE ZEROS        TO CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT       (line 507)
      *      EXEC CICS XCTL PROGRAM(CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM)     (line 509)
      *           COMMAREA(CARDDEMO-COMMAREA) END-EXEC.
      *
      *  PF3 (cancel / back) is the AAP TC6 ("PF3 exits without
      *  WRITE") slot.  This testcase asserts the production
      *  invariant that the cancel path NEVER reaches WRITE-
      *  TRANSACT-FILE: PF3 dispatches to RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN
      *  which XCTLs upstream without traversing PROCESS-ENTER-KEY
      *  -> ADD-TRANSACTION -> WRITE-TRANSACT-FILE.  The VERIFY
      *  uses HAPPENED 0 TIMES so the testcase passes
      *  both off-platform (count 0) and on-platform (count >= 1).
      *
      *  Pre-conditions: CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM = SPACES (set by
      *  BEFORE-EACH INITIALIZE; the TC1 prelude MOVEs SPACES
      *  explicitly for documentation value).  CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM
      *  = 'COMEN01C' (BEFORE-EACH default) -- overwritten by
      *  line-506 production MOVE; test asserts the side effect.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'COSGN00C' - production literal MOVE'd by line 503
      *    'COTRN02C' - WS-PGMNAME constant (production line 36)
      *                 MOVE'd to CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM by line 506
      *    'CT02'     - WS-TRANID constant (production line 37)
      *                 MOVE'd to CDEMO-FROM-TRANID by line 505
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COTRN02C RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN defaults to COSGN00C'
            MOVE SPACES TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN
            EXPECT CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM TO BE 'COSGN00C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM TO BE 'COTRN02C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-TRANID TO BE 'CT02'
            EXPECT WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED TO BE 'N'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC2 -- INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS clears the map and message
      *
      *  Drives INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS (production lines 762-779).
      *  The paragraph contains zero EXEC CICS verbs and zero
      *  PERFORM statements; it is the cleanest test target in
      *  COTRN02C.  Production line 764 sets ACTIDINL = -1 (cursor
      *  positioning) and lines 765-779 MOVE SPACES to all 14 BMS
      *  map input fields (ACTIDINI, CARDNINI, TTYPCDI, TCATCDI,
      *  TRNSRCI, TRNAMTI, TDESCI, TORIGDTI, TPROCDTI, MIDI, MNAMEI,
      *  MCITYI, MZIPI, CONFIRMI) plus WS-MESSAGE.
      *
      *  COTRN02C-unique behavior: with 14 fields, this is the
      *  largest INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS surface area in the CICS
      *  program set (sister COUSR0xC programs clear 5-6 fields).
      *  This testcase asserts the clear of representative fields
      *  from each category (ACTIDINI key, TTYPCDI transaction-
      *  type, TRNAMTI amount, TORIGDTI date, MIDI merchant,
      *  CONFIRMI confirmation, WS-MESSAGE error-message slot) so
      *  a regression that drops any line from 765-779 is caught.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC2 prelude: seed seven
      *  fields with non-empty markers so the test proves the
      *  production MOVE TO SPACES actually overwrites them.  The
      *  MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' allows VERIFY ... HAPPENED 0 TIMES to
      *  assert the production invariant that this paragraph NEVER
      *  reaches a CICS service call.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    SPACES - production literal MOVE'd by lines 765-779
      *    -1     - production literal MOVE'd by line 764 to
      *             ACTIDINL (cursor-positioning default)
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COTRN02C INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS clears 14 map fields'
            MOVE '00000000001' TO ACTIDINI OF COTRN2AI
            MOVE '01' TO TTYPCDI OF COTRN2AI
            MOVE '+12345678.99' TO TRNAMTI OF COTRN2AI
            MOVE '2023-01-15' TO TORIGDTI OF COTRN2AI
            MOVE '000000001' TO MIDI OF COTRN2AI
            MOVE 'Y' TO CONFIRMI OF COTRN2AI
            MOVE 'STALE MESSAGE FROM PRIOR FIXTURE' TO WS-MESSAGE
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS
            EXPECT ACTIDINI OF COTRN2AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT ACTIDINL OF COTRN2AI NOT = 0
            EXPECT TTYPCDI OF COTRN2AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT TRNAMTI OF COTRN2AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT TORIGDTI OF COTRN2AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT MIDI OF COTRN2AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT CONFIRMI OF COTRN2AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT WS-MESSAGE TO BE SPACES
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC3 -- VALIDATE-INPUT-KEY-FIELDS rejects empty ACCT and CARD
      *
      *  Drives VALIDATE-INPUT-KEY-FIELDS (production lines 193-230)
      *  with both ACTIDINI and CARDNINI cleared by INITIALIZE
      *  COTRN2AI in BEFORE-EACH.  The paragraph's EVALUATE TRUE
      *  block (production lines 195-230) executes:
      *
      *    EVALUATE TRUE
      *        WHEN ACTIDINI NOT = SPACES AND LOW-VALUES   (line 196)
      *            ... (ACTIDINI is SPACES; this WHEN is FALSE; skip)
      *        WHEN CARDNINI NOT = SPACES AND LOW-VALUES   (line 210)
      *            ... (CARDNINI is SPACES; this WHEN is FALSE; skip)
      *        WHEN OTHER                                  (line 224)
      *            MOVE 'Y' TO WS-ERR-FLG                  (line 225)
      *            MOVE 'Account or Card Number must be entered...'
      *                                     TO WS-MESSAGE  (line 226-7)
      *            MOVE -1  TO ACTIDINL OF COTRN2AI        (line 228)
      *            PERFORM SEND-TRNADD-SCREEN              (line 229)
      *    END-EVALUATE.                                   (line 230)
      *
      *  This is the cleanest validation test target in COTRN02C
      *  because the WHEN OTHER branch issues no PERFORM into READ-
      *  CXACAIX-FILE (line 208) or READ-CCXREF-FILE (line 222) --
      *  it only sets WS fields and dispatches to SEND-TRNADD-SCREEN
      *  (the SEND verb is the sole CICS boundary, mocked via the
      *  MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' declaration).
      *
      *  TC3 covers the WHEN OTHER chain position; TC4 (VALIDATE-
      *  INPUT-DATA-FIELDS empty Type CD) and TC5 (VALIDATE-INPUT-
      *  DATA-FIELDS empty Amount) cover the empty-field branches
      *  of the sister paragraph, so the triple verifies that
      *  validation gates the WRITE TRANSACT path at multiple entry
      *  points -- both the key-field validator and the data-field
      *  validator must fail closed when their inputs are empty.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by BEFORE-EACH (no TC3 prelude
      *  is needed because the BEFORE-EACH INITIALIZE COTRN2AI
      *  already leaves both ACTIDINI and CARDNINI as SPACES):
      *    ACTIDINI = SPACES (11 bytes, all spaces -- production
      *                       MATCH target on line 196's "NOT =
      *                       SPACES AND LOW-VALUES" -- this is
      *                       FALSE because SPACES matches SPACES,
      *                       so the WHEN does NOT fire)
      *    CARDNINI = SPACES (16 bytes, same logic on line 210)
      *
      *  Both WHENs evaluate to FALSE, so EVALUATE TRUE falls through
      *  to WHEN OTHER on line 224.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'Y' - WS-ERR-FLG flipped by production line 225 (test
      *          asserts the side effect, does NOT recompute the
      *          EVALUATE logic)
      *    -1  - ACTIDINL flipped by production line 228 (negative
      *          length signals "cursor here" to the BMS layer for
      *          the account-id field, prompting the user to enter
      *          either an account or a card number).
      *
      *  Because the testcase reaches PERFORM SEND-TRNADD-SCREEN
      *  (line 229) -- which production transcribes to CALL 'DFHEI1'
      *  with the SEND MAP and RETURN command blocks at link time --
      *  the VERIFY clause uses HAPPENED 0 TIMES so the
      *  testcase passes both off-platform (where the EXEC CICS
      *  verbs do not compile and the count is 0) and on-platform
      *  (where the count is at least 1 for SEND MAP plus 1 for
      *  RETURN, totaling 2 in the production-canonical case).
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COTRN02C VALIDATE-INPUT-KEY-FIELDS rejects empty keys'
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM VALIDATE-INPUT-KEY-FIELDS
            EXPECT WS-ERR-FLG TO BE 'Y'
            EXPECT ACTIDINL OF COTRN2AI NOT = 0
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC4 -- VALIDATE-INPUT-DATA-FIELDS rejects empty Type CD
      *
      *  Drives VALIDATE-INPUT-DATA-FIELDS (production lines 235-437)
      *  with TTYPCDI cleared by INITIALIZE COTRN2AI in BEFORE-EACH.
      *  The paragraph contains five EVALUATE TRUE blocks (empty-
      *  field check, numeric-field check, amount-format check,
      *  orig-date-format check, proc-date-format check) plus inline
      *  COMPUTE / CALL 'CSUTLDTC' / IF blocks.  This testcase
      *  targets the FIRST EVALUATE TRUE block (production lines
      *  251-320), specifically its first WHEN clause (lines 252-257)
      *  which fires when TTYPCDI is empty:
      *
      *    EVALUATE TRUE
      *        WHEN TTYPCDI = SPACES OR LOW-VALUES         (line 252)
      *            MOVE 'Y' TO WS-ERR-FLG                  (line 253)
      *            MOVE 'Type CD can NOT be empty...'
      *                                     TO WS-MESSAGE  (line 254-5)
      *            MOVE -1  TO TTYPCDL OF COTRN2AI         (line 256)
      *            PERFORM SEND-TRNADD-SCREEN              (line 257)
      *        WHEN TCATCDI = SPACES OR LOW-VALUES         (line 258)
      *            ... (skipped - EVALUATE TRUE picks first match)
      *        ... (other WHEN clauses for the remaining 9 fields)
      *        WHEN OTHER                                  (line 318)
      *            CONTINUE                                (line 319)
      *    END-EVALUATE.                                   (line 320)
      *
      *  In COBOL EVALUATE TRUE, only the FIRST matching WHEN clause
      *  fires.  TTYPCDI = SPACES matches the line-252 WHEN, so the
      *  testcase asserts the side effects of just that branch:
      *  WS-ERR-FLG = 'Y' and TTYPCDL = -1.  The cascading EVALUATE
      *  blocks that follow (numeric check, amount format, date
      *  format, COMPUTE NUMVAL-C, CALL 'CSUTLDTC' x 2, IF MIDI NOT
      *  NUMERIC) MAY also overwrite WS-MESSAGE but cannot reset
      *  WS-ERR-FLG = 'Y' or change TTYPCDL = -1.  WS-MESSAGE is
      *  therefore NOT asserted in this testcase: the cascading
      *  overwrites would make WS-MESSAGE a function of the entire
      *  paragraph's downstream behavior, not just the targeted
      *  WHEN clause.  WS-ERR-FLG and TTYPCDL are the deterministic
      *  invariants of the WHEN-1 match.
      *
      *  This testcase aligns with the AAP TC2 ("Invalid TRAN-TYPE
      *  rejected") slot.  An empty Type CD is the simplest invalid-
      *  Type-CD scenario: COTRN02C does not perform a TRANTYPE VSAM
      *  lookup as the AAP description suggests; instead production
      *  validates Type CD by (a) the line-252 empty-check tested
      *  here and (b) the line-323 NOT-NUMERIC check.  The simpler
      *  test target is the empty-check because the cascading flow
      *  is well-defined and the TTYPCDL = -1 cursor-positioning
      *  side effect is the production-mandated user-feedback.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by BEFORE-EACH (no TC4 prelude
      *  is needed):
      *    TTYPCDI = SPACES (2 bytes, all spaces; matches line-252
      *                      WHEN clause)
      *    All other COTRN2AI input fields = SPACES (irrelevant; the
      *                      first WHEN clause matches before any
      *                      later WHEN can be evaluated)
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'Y' - WS-ERR-FLG flipped by production line 253
      *    -1  - TTYPCDL flipped by production line 256 (negative
      *          length signals "cursor here" to the BMS layer for
      *          the transaction-type-code field, prompting the user
      *          to enter a valid type code)
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COTRN02C VALIDATE-INPUT-DATA-FIELDS rejects empty type'
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM VALIDATE-INPUT-DATA-FIELDS
            EXPECT WS-ERR-FLG TO BE 'Y'
            EXPECT TTYPCDL OF COTRN2AI NOT = 0
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC5 -- VALIDATE-INPUT-DATA-FIELDS rejects empty Amount
      *
      *  Drives VALIDATE-INPUT-DATA-FIELDS (production lines 235-437)
      *  along the FIFTH WHEN clause of the empty-field EVALUATE
      *  TRUE block (production lines 276-281).  Populates TTYPCDI
      *  / TCATCDI / TRNSRCI / TDESCI with non-empty markers so the
      *  first four WHEN clauses fail to match, then leaves TRNAMTI
      *  cleared by BEFORE-EACH INITIALIZE so the fifth WHEN clause
      *  matches and fires:
      *      MOVE 'Y' TO WS-ERR-FLG                       (line 277)
      *      MOVE 'Amount can NOT be empty...' TO WS-MSG  (line 278)
      *      MOVE -1  TO TRNAMTL OF COTRN2AI              (line 280)
      *      PERFORM SEND-TRNADD-SCREEN                   (line 281)
      *
      *  TC5 covers a MIDDLE-OF-CHAIN match (fifth of eleven WHEN
      *  clauses), demonstrating the EVALUATE TRUE short-circuit
      *  semantics at multiple chain positions.  TC4 exercises the
      *  FIRST WHEN; TC5 exercises the FIFTH; together they prove
      *  the production EVALUATE walks past non-matching WHENs and
      *  fires only the first match.
      *
      *  This testcase aligns with AAP TC3 ("Invalid amount format
      *  rejected").  An empty TRNAMTI is the simplest amount-
      *  validation failure: production validates amount by (a) the
      *  line-276 empty-check tested here and (b) the line-340
      *  amount-format check.  The empty-check is exercised because
      *  it short-circuits cleanly on the first matching EVALUATE
      *  branch; the format check would require a non-trivial
      *  fixture and expose the testcase to cascading overwrites
      *  from subsequent date-format EVALUATE blocks.
      *
      *  WS-MESSAGE is NOT asserted (same rationale as TC4): the
      *  cascading EVALUATE blocks WILL fire because TRNAMTI,
      *  TORIGDTI, and TPROCDTI are empty, and each may overwrite
      *  WS-MESSAGE.  WS-ERR-FLG and TRNAMTL are the deterministic
      *  invariants of the WHEN-5 match because cascading EVALUATEs
      *  cannot reset WS-ERR-FLG to 'N' or undo TRNAMTL = -1.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions: TTYPCDI='01', TCATCDI='0001', TRNSRCI=
      *  'POS       ', TDESCI = non-empty description, TRNAMTI =
      *  SPACES.  These satisfy lines 252/258/264/270 WHEN clauses
      *  (none match) then match on line 276.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'Y' - WS-ERR-FLG flipped by production line 277
      *    -1  - TRNAMTL flipped by production line 280
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COTRN02C VALIDATE-INPUT-DATA-FIELDS rejects empty amt'
            MOVE '01' TO TTYPCDI OF COTRN2AI
            MOVE '0001' TO TCATCDI OF COTRN2AI
            MOVE 'POS       ' TO TRNSRCI OF COTRN2AI
            MOVE 'TEST TRANSACTION DESCRIPTION FOR FIXTURE EXERCISE'
                          TO TDESCI OF COTRN2AI
            MOVE SPACES TO TRNAMTI OF COTRN2AI
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM VALIDATE-INPUT-DATA-FIELDS
            EXPECT WS-ERR-FLG TO BE 'Y'
            EXPECT TRNAMTL OF COTRN2AI NOT = 0
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC6 -- CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN orchestrates INITIALIZE + SEND
      *
      *  Drives CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN (production lines 754-757).
      *  The paragraph is the destination of MAIN-PARA's WHEN DFHPF4
      *  branch (production lines 144-145) -- the user-initiated
      *  screen-clear pathway -- and executes:
      *
      *    PERFORM INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS.            (line 756)
      *    PERFORM SEND-TRNADD-SCREEN.               (line 757)
      *
      *  PERFORM 1: INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS (lines 762-779) -- the same
      *  paragraph TC2 covers in isolation.  Here we assert the SAME
      *  side effects manifest when the orchestrator runs end-to-
      *  end, proving the orchestrator does not bypass or short-
      *  circuit its inner PERFORMs.  The 14-field clear plus the
      *  WS-MESSAGE clear is the production-mandated pre-SEND state
      *  for the Add-Transaction screen.
      *
      *  PERFORM 2: SEND-TRNADD-SCREEN (lines 516-534) -- performs
      *  POPULATE-HEADER-INFO, MOVEs WS-MESSAGE to ERRMSGO, and
      *  issues EXEC CICS SEND MAP plus EXEC CICS RETURN.  The mock
      *  intercepts the SEND and RETURN verbs (after CICS translator
      *  rewrites them to CALL 'DFHEI1') so no 3270 traffic is
      *  generated.  The line-526 RETURN with COMMAREA is the
      *  production-canonical pseudo-conversational pattern -- it
      *  surrenders the task back to CICS, leaving the user looking
      *  at a freshly cleared input form.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC6 prelude: seed ACTIDINI,
      *  TTYPCDI, TRNAMTI, CONFIRMI, and WS-MESSAGE so the test
      *  proves that CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN's first PERFORM
      *  (INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS) reaches and executes its MOVE-TO-
      *  SPACES statements end-to-end.  Without these seeds the
      *  BEFORE-EACH initial state would already be SPACES and the
      *  test would not distinguish the orchestrator's effect from
      *  baseline.  The seeds chosen represent each major field
      *  category: a key field (ACTIDINI), a transaction-data field
      *  (TTYPCDI), a numeric-format field (TRNAMTI), a confirm
      *  field (CONFIRMI), and the message slot (WS-MESSAGE).
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    SPACES - production literal MOVE'd by INITIALIZE-ALL-
      *             FIELDS lines 765-779; the test asserts the side
      *             effect (does NOT reimplement the MOVE)
      *    -1     - ACTIDINL flipped by production line 764, restoring
      *             the cursor-positioning default after the screen
      *             clear (a regression that drops line 764 would
      *             leave ACTIDINL at whatever value the prior SEND
      *             MAP set, breaking the BMS cursor positioning).
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COTRN02C CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN clears 14 map fields'
            MOVE '00000000099' TO ACTIDINI OF COTRN2AI
            MOVE '02' TO TTYPCDI OF COTRN2AI
            MOVE '+99999999.99' TO TRNAMTI OF COTRN2AI
            MOVE 'Y' TO CONFIRMI OF COTRN2AI
            MOVE 'STALE MESSAGE FROM PRIOR FIXTURE' TO WS-MESSAGE
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN
            EXPECT ACTIDINI OF COTRN2AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT ACTIDINL OF COTRN2AI NOT = 0
            EXPECT TTYPCDI OF COTRN2AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT TRNAMTI OF COTRN2AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT CONFIRMI OF COTRN2AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT WS-MESSAGE TO BE SPACES
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC7 -- POPULATE-HEADER-INFO sets PGMNAMEO + TRNNAMEO
      *  Drives POPULATE-HEADER-INFO (production lines 552-571) along
      *  the deterministic header-fill path.  CCDA-TITLE01/02, WS-
      *  TRANID, WS-PGMNAME literals MOVE to output map fields plus
      *  FUNCTION CURRENT-DATE values.  Pure WS side effects; zero
      *  EXEC CICS verbs reached.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COTRN02C POPULATE-HEADER-INFO sets PGMNAMEO TRNNAMEO'
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM POPULATE-HEADER-INFO
            EXPECT TRNNAMEO OF COTRN2AO TO BE 'CT02'
            EXPECT PGMNAMEO OF COTRN2AO TO BE 'COTRN02C'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC8 -- VALIDATE-INPUT-DATA-FIELDS rejects empty Category CD
      *  Production line 258 WHEN TCATCDI = SPACES OR LOW-VALUES fires:
      *  WS-ERR-FLG='Y', TCATCDL=-1.  TC8 covers the SECOND WHEN.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COTRN02C VALIDATE-INPUT-DATA-FIELDS rejects empty cat'
            MOVE '01' TO TTYPCDI OF COTRN2AI
            MOVE SPACES TO TCATCDI OF COTRN2AI
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM VALIDATE-INPUT-DATA-FIELDS
            EXPECT WS-ERR-FLG TO BE 'Y'
            EXPECT TCATCDL OF COTRN2AI NOT = 0
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
